 "standard_url": "https://www.deped.gov.ph/wp-content/uploads/MATATAG-Mathematics-CG-Grades1-4-and-7.pdf",
 "standard_text": "Describe given rational numbers as fractions, decimals, or percentages.",
 "meta_desc": "Free Grade 7 fractions, decimals and percentages worksheets for the DepEd MATATAG curriculum: converting, equivalent forms and ordering rational numbers. 100 questions with answers.",
 "key_big": "Fraction → decimal: divide. Decimal → percent: × 100.",
 "key_sub": "To order, change all to decimals.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li>A <b>rational number</b> can be written as a fraction <span class='fr'><span class='fn'>a</span><span class='fd'>b</span></span> of integers (b ≠ 0). It can also be written as a decimal or a percentage.</li><li>Fraction → decimal: divide the numerator by the denominator. <span class='fr'><span class='fn'>3</span><span class='fd'>8</span></span> = 3 ÷ 8 = 0.375.</li><li>Decimal → percentage: multiply by 100. 0.375 = 37.5%.</li><li>To order, change all the numbers to decimals.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'><span class='fr'><span class='fn'>3</span><span class='fd'>5</span></span></p><p class='sn-ex-s'>3 ÷ 5 = 0.6</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>0.6 × 100</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 60%</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3/8 as 3.8</td><td>Divide: 3 ÷ 8 = 0.375.</td></tr><tr><td>0.6 as 6%</td><td>0.6 = 60%.</td></tr><tr><td>Comparing digits</td><td>Write all as decimals first.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "What does MATATAG Math 7 ask about rational numbers?",
   "a": "Describe given rational numbers as fractions, decimals, or percentages."
  },
  {
   "q": "Is 0.333… rational?",
   "a": "Yes. It equals 1/3."
  },
  {
   "q": "How do I write 45% as a fraction?",
   "a": "45/100 = 9/20."
  },
  {
   "q": "Which is bigger, 5/8 or 0.6?",
   "a": "5/8 = 0.625, so 5/8."
  }
 ],
